WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:03.190
Earlier today I received orders from my superior.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:07.830
I am being sent to investigate a mysterious
SCP located under a warehouse on the outskirts

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:08.830
of London.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:13.460
It seems important as the SCP was just discovered
and the Overseer Council wants a detailed

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.780
report on it right away.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.670
I pull up outside of the Port Superior Canning
Company warehouse.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:22.310
It is abandoned, and from the look of it,
has been for a long time.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.409
I enter the building and make my way to an
opening at the far side of the warehouse.

00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:30.099
I descend the narrow stairwell where I see
a small black door.

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:34.060
I was told there was always a guard posted
by the door, but there is no one here.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.930
I stop just outside the black door and look
up.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:42.680
Above the door handle is a placard that says:
"SCP Foundation Department of Abnormalities.”

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.090
I am in the right place, but nothing feels
right.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.680
Maybe I should just turn around and tell my
superior I couldn’t find the door.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.180
I take a deep breath, grab the handle, and
turn.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.750
The door doesn’t budge.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.350
I step back for a moment and take a breath
of relief.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:02.510
Then I glance to the side of the door and
see the sliding lock—my stomach sinks.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.979
I move the metal rod aside and try the door
again.

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:08.039
This time it swings open.

00:01:08.039 --> 00:01:12.340
I shake my head in dismay and walk in to the
other side of the black door.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.670
I have now entered SCP-3790.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.490
A series of dim emergency lights flicker on.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.810
There are four doors.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.429
On the other side of the hallway is an elevator.

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:23.499
“Hello?”

00:01:23.499 --> 00:01:25.890
I say only slightly louder than a whisper.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.500
There is no response.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.749
I walk along the grated floor,
the metal rattles under my boots.

00:01:31.749 --> 00:01:36.100
I can see through the grating and it appears
there are several floors below me.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.609
I come to the first door and examine it.

00:01:38.609 --> 00:01:40.460
All of the doors are identical.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.159
They are made up of heavy metal, a sliding
panel that covers a glass viewport, and placards

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:47.049
that identify what is in the room.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:51.509
All of the handles to the doors have been
broken off, and the doors themselves have

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:53.090
been welded shut.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.350
It seems that whoever abandoned the Department
of Abnormalities wanted to make sure whatever

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.670
is in these rooms never got out.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:03.920
As I stare into the room I begin to feel something
well up inside of me.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.810
I zone out for a moment.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:11.310
When I regain my bearings my hand has moved
itself to the spot where the door handle once

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:17.319
was; as if while I was in my daze something
tried to trick me into opening the door.

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:21.939
I immediately shove my hands into my pockets,
turn, and walk back toward the black door

00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:24.090
to get out of this place.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.840
Something is not right here.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.190
As I approach the exit, the door slams shut.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.910
I race over to it and try turning the knob.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.130
It will not budge.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:35.129
I have been locked in SCP-3790.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:39.489
I begin to panic as my eyes dart from door
to door, scanning for a way out.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:43.790
There is nowhere to go but deeper into The
Department of Abnormalities.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.970
I glance down to my right and notice something
lying on the ground.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.230
It’s a clipboard.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.410
I pick it up and skim through the pages of
the legal pad that is attached to it.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:57.110
Most of what is written seems like the ravings
of a madman, but on one page there are some

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.519
coherent notes.

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:00.980
It says: “Think it's about time.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.390
Need to lock down the other sites before I
go.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.390
Take care.”

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.680
There is a list of ten roman numerals with
either the word “locked” or “unlocked”

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.880
beside them.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.010
VII, VIII, and X all remain unlocked.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.920
I am not sure if this is a good or bad thing,
but it seems that whoever was here before

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.730
me is now on their way to complete what they
started.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:26.540
I toss the clipboard and look down the corridor
hoping that a magical door will appear and

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.340
let me out of the Department of Abnormalities.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:34.739
After several minutes I decide to explore
SCP-3790 more thoroughly; perhaps there is

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:37.090
another way out on a different level.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:41.470
This gets my hopes up slightly, but part of
me believes this will be where I spend the

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.549
rest of my short life.

00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:47.430
I walk back up to the door where I think I
hear music coming from.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.349
I wipe the dust and grime off the placard
and read what it says.

00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:53.849
The name written on it is “Vivaldi.”

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:57.090
I slide the panel away from the viewport and
look inside.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.319
The chamber is completely empty except for
one object.

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:04.379
In the far corner of the room, a violin is
propped up against the wall.

00:04:04.379 --> 00:04:06.629
In front of it is a broken bow.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:10.819
I squint my eyes to get a better look at the
instrument; it seems normal enough.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:15.469
Suddenly, an uneasy feeling comes over me,
like I am being watched.

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:18.959
I whip the panel closed over the viewport
and back away from the door.

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:21.769
I turn down the hallway and walk to the next
door.

00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:25.100
The name on the placard for this room is “Montezuma’s
Face.”

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:29.800
I’m a little hesitant to open the panel
and peer inside because of what might be looking

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:30.800
back at me.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.300
I take a breath to build a bit of courage,
and go for it.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.560
I slide the panel open, and to my relief,
all that is on the other side of the viewport

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.510
is an empty room with a metal table in the
center.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.259
On it rests an ornate wooden chest.

00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:47.389
The chest has been secured with a large steel
padlock.

00:04:47.389 --> 00:04:50.940
I put my face a little closer to the glass
to try and get a better look at the markings

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:51.960
on the chest.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:56.770
I can hear a faint clicking sound like that
of a ticking clock coming from the room.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.030
Other than that, all is still.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.140
I shrug and check the next door.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:04.780
To my surprise, the next room has had its
placard removed.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.360
When I peer into the viewport the room is
completely empty.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:12.190
This is strange as this door has also been
welded shut.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:17.150
The fourth door in the corridor has had its
placard damaged, making the text on it unreadable.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.819
I slide the panel open and look inside.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:24.860
There appears to be nothing there, but upon
closer inspection, I see that the concrete

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.180
walls are covered in claw marks.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:32.540
It looks like whatever was in this chamber
had incredibly sharp talons, and was not happy

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.420
about being detained.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:38.690
On the floor are pieces of bone that have
had the meat picked clean from them.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:44.230
Each room is another mystery but offers no
way out of the Department of Abnormalities.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.740
My only hope is to go deeper into the facility.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.199
I push the button for the elevator.

00:05:49.199 --> 00:05:51.350
The door chimes and slides open.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.910
I step inside and look at the seven buttons
on the panel.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.080
Next to each one is the level number it corresponds
to.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.740
Naturally I'm hesitant to push any of them,
but I know i’ve got to start somewhere if

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.220
i’m going to have any chance of getting
out of here.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.599
I reach out and press the button for Level
2.

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:12.990
The doors slide shut and the elevator descends
deeper into the depths of the Department of

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.520
Abnormalities.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.830
The elevator comes to a stop and the doors
slide open.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.289
I step out into another corridor.

00:06:20.289 --> 00:06:24.819
It seems identical to the first one except
there is no black door on the opposite side

00:06:24.819 --> 00:06:26.050
of the hallway.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.720
This worries me a little, but I continue on.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.639
According to the placard on the first door
of Level 2, the room contains a man named

00:06:33.639 --> 00:06:34.639
Ian.

00:06:34.639 --> 00:06:37.360
I slide the panel open and look through the
viewport.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.250
In the corner of the room sits a thin, pale,
man wearing a dirty straightjacket.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.069
He is blindfolded and does not seem to notice
me.

00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:47.340
His chest moves slowly up and down.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.640
I feel bad for the man being cooped up in
there all alone.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.449
But then again, I have no idea what Ian is
capable of.

00:06:54.449 --> 00:06:59.069
The second room on this level contains something
called The Crying Boy.

00:06:59.069 --> 00:07:03.360
When I look into the chamber I expect to see
a young child weeping; instead, there appears

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.750
to be a painting on an easel in the middle
of the room.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.169
It has a sheet draped over it so I can not
see what is on the canvas, but from inside

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:15.050
the room, I can hear the sobs of a small child.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:18.910
The placard for the third room indicates the
creatures that are contained within it are

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.620
called “The Watchers.”

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.630
When I look into the chamber, I see three
humanoid figures huddled together.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.780
They are all staring towards the far corner
with their backs turned toward me.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.849
The creatures sway back and forth slowly.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:33.750
It’s an unsettling sight to say the least.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:38.259
One that will be difficult to forget, and
will definitely haunt my dreams.

00:07:38.259 --> 00:07:40.819
The fourth door on Level 2 has no placard.

00:07:40.819 --> 00:07:45.129
When I look inside I see another dark hallway
similar to the one I’m in.

00:07:45.129 --> 00:07:49.909
I try to force the door open as it might be
a way out, but like all the rest, it has been

00:07:49.909 --> 00:07:51.120
welded shut.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.509
I kick the metal door hoping and wishfully
thinking it will make an impact, but instead

00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:57.780
I instantly regret my decision.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:02.780
I contemplate my extreme lack of karate skills
as I limp back to the elevator in defeat.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:05.330
I descend to the third level.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:09.039
Room one on Level 3 contains something called
The Infinite Cold.

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:12.629
When I look into the chamber I can see that
the floor is covered with a thin layer of

00:08:12.629 --> 00:08:13.629
ice.

00:08:13.629 --> 00:08:17.699
What is odd is that the interior of the room
seems to go on forever in all directions.

00:08:17.699 --> 00:08:22.470
It even appears to extend to the room next
to it, but when I look into the viewport to

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:27.780
the second room there is a solid wall between
The Infinite Cold and the empty pedestal in

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:28.789
room two.

00:08:28.789 --> 00:08:33.470
I check the placard for the second room and
find that it is called “Sorrow.”

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:37.479
It looks like there was once something on
top of the pedestal, but the four finger marks

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:42.450
left in the dust that now covers it indicates
the object had been removed recently.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:45.300
The third room is named “World Without Man.”

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.330
Unsurprisingly the chamber is completely empty.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.990
The fourth room on this level is labeled “Adam’s
Hatred.”

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:56.240
This does not seem like something I want to
see, but I slide the panel away from the viewport

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.360
and glance in anyway.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:04.269
In the back of the room is a large black mass
slowly oscillating in mid-air; I feel anger

00:09:04.269 --> 00:09:05.700
begin to fill me.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:11.200
The rage of this creature is palpable; it’s
being transferred from the black mass to me.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:17.230
Scared of what it, or I, might do, I run back
to the elevator and hit the button for Level

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:18.230
4.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:22.230
On the placard of the first room on Level
4 are the words “The Morning Star.”

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:25.970
All that is in the chamber is a rusted sword
hanging from the wall.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:30.930
However, as I move my face closer to the window
to get a better look, the temperature starts

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.130
to rise.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.839
It feels like the fires of hell are just on
the other side of this door.

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:41.050
The placard for the next room is labeled “Wormwood,”
but when I open the panel to peer inside there

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:43.050
is something obstructing my view.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:46.160
I don’t spend much time here, and move onto
the next.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.080
The placard on door three names this anomaly
as “Harmonia’s Necklace.”

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:55.050
Within the chamber, a golden chain hangs from
a post against the back wall.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:10:00.230
A single candle burns just beneath the necklace,
illuminating the space around it.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:04.570
When I look closer at the candle I realize
the chamber has no floor.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:08.080
The light seems to be floating among infinite
darkness.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.910
The fourth chamber on this level has no placard.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.000
When I look inside, the room is unlit.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:18.820
All I feel is a sense of dread - A feeling
that follows me all the way back to the elevator.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.050
I descend to Level 5.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.519
The first door is labeled as “The Heart
of Man.”

00:10:24.519 --> 00:10:29.339
Inside is a human heart suspended in midair
by a wire hanging from the ceiling.

00:10:29.339 --> 00:10:33.470
I look closer, and to my horror, I see the
heart is still beating.

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:39.399
The entire room starts to distort, my own
heart aches; I run down the hallway to the

00:10:39.399 --> 00:10:40.480
second door.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.850
The placard for this room has been pried off.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:47.450
The word “hello” has been scratched into
the metal where the label once was.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:51.829
When I try to slide the panel over to look
into the room I find that just like the door

00:10:51.829 --> 00:10:55.740
itself, the panel has also been welded shut.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.850
Whatever is on the other side of this door
must be truly terrible.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:02.750
The third door contains something called “Channel
55.”

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:07.440
In the room there is a small CRT television
set under a dark cloth.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:11.550
I can see the light from the tv shining through
the sheet, but cannot make out the image on

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:12.550
the screen.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:17.470
The fourth door of floor 5 has a placard with
the words “Living Nightmare” printed on

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:18.470
it.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:21.730
I pause for a moment to think if I really
want to see what is inside this room.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:26.390
I figure I’ve come this far, and maybe it’s
just a trick to keep me from finding the exit.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.240
I slowly slide the panel away from the viewport.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:33.389
It makes a sound like a creaky door opening
in a haunted house.

00:11:33.389 --> 00:11:36.800
In the room there is a bed resting on a metal
frame.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.829
Someone appears to be lying on the bed with
a sheet pulled up over their head.

00:11:40.829 --> 00:11:42.220
Creepy, I think.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:47.260
I walk back to the elevator and cannot help
but feel I am about to reach something terrifyingly

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.560
significant in my journey.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.740
One way or another, whatever is on the next
two floors will seal my fate.

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:55.519
I get off on level six.

00:11:55.519 --> 00:11:58.740
It looks identical to all of the previous
floors.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:02.490
The first room contains something called “Mister
Silence.”

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.230
Resting on the back chamber wall is a tall
wooden box.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:09.380
It has been painted black with a purple “W”
adorning the front of it.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.690
I hold my breath for a moment.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.260
It’s so quiet that the silence hurts my
ears.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:17.360
The second room contains “The Dead Man’s
Chair.”

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.820
In the corner of the chamber is a wooden seat.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:24.649
There is no one sitting on it, but as I look
at the shadow against the wall there is clearly

00:12:24.649 --> 00:12:26.360
a figure seated there.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:30.970
I glance back at the wooden chair, but it
is still empty, and upon a second look at

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.430
the shadow, the figure is gone.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:35.680
The placard on the third door reads “Ötzi.”

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:39.180
When I slide open the viewport it is covered
in ice.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:43.339
I can’t see completely through the ice,
but from what I can make out there seems to

00:12:43.339 --> 00:12:46.380
be a dark shape standing in the middle of
the room.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:49.769
The fourth door on Level 6 contains “Apollyon’s
Crown.”

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:52.540
There are scratch marks all across the metal
door.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:56.880
It looks as if something was trying to get
into the room instead of out of it.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:01.120
In the chamber itself is a silver lockbox
resting on a table.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.910
Whatever is inside must be very important
to someone.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:07.490
I enter the elevator and press the button
for Level 7.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:12.199
The doors slide shut and the elevator begins
to descend to the bottom level.

00:13:12.199 --> 00:13:16.990
I know that if there is no way out on this
floor, I will be trapped like all of the other

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:20.070
objects in the Department of Abnormalities.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:24.390
The bell chimes indicating I’ve reached
what I hope is my way out of here.

00:13:24.390 --> 00:13:25.839
The doors slide open.

00:13:25.839 --> 00:13:29.270
I take a few steps out into a corridor that
looks like all the rest.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.650
I turn and gaze into the first room on the
floor.

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:36.590
Instantly, terror fills every centimeter of
space in my core.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.760
It feels as if my heart stops.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:42.440
Frozen in fear for a moment, I try to scream
but nothing escapes.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.220
I come to my senses and am able to use my
legs again.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.510
I run back to the elevator and hit the button
for the first floor.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:52.779
As the elevator ascends back up to where I
began this nightmarish tour, my body trembles

00:13:52.779 --> 00:13:54.130
more and more.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:58.160
As soon as the elevator chimes at Level 1,
without hesitation, and with my shaking hands

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:02.949
and nimble fingers, I immediately rip open
the button panel and tear out the wires connected

00:14:02.949 --> 00:14:04.230
to Level 7.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:09.450
No one should ever have to see what is that
far down in the Department of Abnormalities,

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.130
and now no one ever will.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:16.130
Now watch “SCP-5545 - Mysterious Tunnels
in Antarctica - ABNORMALITY.”

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.370
Or check out “25 Most Frightening SCP.”

